  [1mOne thing to keep in view[0m

  Everything here persists a username someone typed into a text box. The design is honest about that — [38;5;153msource: [39m
  [38;5;153m"client-asserted"[39m, documented in the module header — but no amount of structure makes it authenticated. It's sound for
  greeting a user, prefilling forms, or client-side convenience. It is not an audit trail, and it must not gate
  anything that matters until a server is vouching for the value. I'll state that in the spec's constraints so future
  consumers meet it before they misuse it.

  Does this look right? If so I'll write it up as a spec, run it through self-review and the Codex spec gate, and hand
  it to you to read before any code gets written.

